  "answer": "Requests combines hooks in Session.prepare_request() at line 496 using merge_hooks(request.hooks, self.hooks). merge_hooks treats an empty response-hook list specially: if the session has no response hooks, it returns the request hooks; if the request has no response hooks, it returns the session hooks. If both contain response hooks, merge_setting() is used, with session hooks as the base and request hooks taking precedence for duplicate keys. The hook lists are not concatenated; a request-level response hook list replaces the session-level list when both are non-empty. By default, request hooks are usually {'response': []}, so session response hooks are preserved.",
